<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φᾰτός</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φημί</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spoken</i> or <i>that
				may be spoken,</i> mostly with negat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ φ.</span> un<i>speakable,</i> un<i>utterable,</i>
				in<i>effable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				230
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				8.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				7(6).37
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μὴ φ. μηδὲ ῥητὸν κάλλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.383a
				</span></i>
			; pleon., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλλος οὐ φ. λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1713
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ φατῶς,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφάτως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>famous, notable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρες ἄφατοί τε φ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
